<title>PORTUGAL: PORTUGUESE BOND REPORT.</title>
<headline>PORTUGUESE BOND REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese bonds rose in brisk trade with medium maturities particularly strong and dealers expected further gains during the session.</p>
<p>Traders said fears of interest rate hikes in the U.S. and Germany had diminished and this was helping prices but the market was still highly sensitive to dollar movements.</p>
<p>&quot;Financial investors are buying across the curve but the medium maturities are in most demand,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The escudo was little changed at 101.20/22 per mark.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
